message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Malaysian Motor BI Reserving: Dissertation Analysis Code"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kubilius"
    given-names: "Jason"
    affiliation: "Queen Mary University of London"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  Code supporting the MSc dissertation "Projecting Malaysian Motor BI Excess
  Claims: Chain Ladder Benchmarks and an Integrated Claim-Level Machine
  Learning Framework". The repository contains the data-processing,
  Random Forest, XGBoost, historical back-testing, pure IBNR and out-of-time
  validation workflows used in the dissertation. The underlying Malaysian
  Motor claims data are confidential and are not included.
keywords:
  - actuarial science
  - claims reserving
  - machine learning
  - Random Forest
  - XGBoost
  - Chain Ladder
  - bodily injury
  - insurance
